Adds projectm_set_frame_time() to libprojectM 4.1.8, so an application can
set the time of each frame instead of projectM reading the system clock.
VizX needs this to pre-render frames at a fixed frame rate.

The function has the same name and meaning as the one in projectM's
development branch; drop this patch once a release contains it.

Apply from the libprojectM source folder:  git apply <this file>

diff --git a/src/api/include/projectM-4/parameters.h b/src/api/include/projectM-4/parameters.h
index 2d9c70c..c238a92 100644
--- a/src/api/include/projectM-4/parameters.h
+++ b/src/api/include/projectM-4/parameters.h
@@ -229,6 +229,19 @@ PROJECTM_EXPORT bool projectm_get_aspect_correction(projectm_handle instance);
  */
 PROJECTM_EXPORT void projectm_set_easter_egg(projectm_handle instance, float value);
 
+/**
+ * @brief Sets the time of the next rendered frame.
+ *
+ * <p>By default, projectM measures time with the system clock. For offline rendering at a
+ * fixed frame rate, set the time of each frame explicitly before rendering it, so the result
+ * does not depend on how long rendering takes.</p>
+ *
+ * @param instance The projectM instance handle.
+ * @param seconds_since_first_frame Time in seconds since the first frame. Pass a negative
+ *                                  value to return to the system clock.
+ */
+PROJECTM_EXPORT void projectm_set_frame_time(projectm_handle instance, double seconds_since_first_frame);
+
 /**
  * @brief Returns the current "easter egg" value.
  * @param instance The projectM instance handle.
